  "id": "COMPOUND:43678 - PROTEIN:6150",
  "verbalization": "Mycamamide D appears to interact with H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3 through a series of molecular targets that are involved in sialyltransferase activity and the metabolism of specific compounds. The evidence suggests that Mycalamide D acts as a target of multiple compounds, including 2-Methylheptyl propanoate and Hydroxy-Alpha-Sanshool, which in turn target the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. This implies a potential pathway where Mycalamide D indirectly influences the transporter through its interaction with these intermediates. The shared involvement of sialyltransferase activity in the targeting process suggests a possible mechanism involving enzymatic regulation or metabolic modulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, where Mycalamide D may exert its effects through a chain of molecular interactions that ultimately modulate the function of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3.",
